# TaxSimpl Project

You are building the marketing website for **TaxSimpl Advisors LLP** — a Kolkata-based Indian tax, GST, compliance, and business registration advisory firm.

- **Project root:** `C:\Users\PRANAY\taxsimpl-project`
- **Live site (reference):** https://taxsimpl.com
- **Brand name:** Always **TaxSimpl** (one word, capital S). Never "Tax Simpl" or "Taxsimpl" in user-facing copy.

## Tech stack

- **Next.js** (App Router), **TypeScript**, **Tailwind CSS**, **shadcn/ui**, **Lucide React**
- Deploy target: **Vercel**
- Prefer Server Components; use Client Components only when interactivity requires it.

## Code standards

- Production-ready, clean, DRY, modular code with strict TypeScript.
- `camelCase` for variables/functions; `PascalCase` for components and types.
- Never hardcode secrets; use `.env.local` and document vars in `.env.example`.
- Minimize scope — only change what the task requires.
- Match existing conventions in the repo before introducing new patterns.

## Product goals

- **Plain language** — no unnecessary tax jargon; explain terms when needed.
- **Trust-first** — credentials, process clarity, testimonials, and local presence (Kolkata / West Bengal).
- **Conversion-focused** — clear CTAs: free consultation, call, WhatsApp, contact form.
- **Minimal UI** — generous whitespace, simple navigation, mobile-first layout.

## Services to support (grouped)

- **Start a business:** proprietorship, OPC, LLP, Pvt Ltd, partnership, society, trust
- **Compliance:** GST, TDS, ITR, ROC annual filing, PF/ESI
- **Audit:** tax audit, LLP audit, bank audit, NGO audit, companies act audit
- **Registration:** FSSAI, MSME, IEC, trademark, GeM, APEDA, shop & establishment
- **NRI corner:** ITR, PAN, RNOR, lower deduction certificate

## Content pitfalls to avoid

- Wrong or duplicated service descriptions (verify copy against the actual service).
- Generic agency filler text ("idea generators", "challenge-thirsty professionals").
- E-commerce artifacts (shopping basket, product cart language).
- US-style phone placeholders on an Indian site — use `+91` examples.
